# codex-lens.config: fixed contract and operational knobs for the Codex cross-model review lens.
#
# Read by scripts/codex-lens.sh (the /codex-lens skill and review-panel Step 2.6). This file is
# sourced by bash. Keep it to assignments and comments, no logic.
#
# TWO CLASSES of value, and it matters which is which:
#   - The REVIEW CONTRACT (the sandbox) uses HARD assignment (`=`), so sourcing this file OVERWRITES
#     any pre-set environment variable of the same name: a stray CODEX_LENS_SANDBOX=workspace-write in
#     someone's shell must NOT make the review write-capable.
#   - The OPERATIONAL KNOBS (caps, thresholds) use assign-if-unset (`:=`), so a pre-set env var wins,
#     for one-off runs. These cannot weaken the review; they only bound how long it runs and how it
#     packages the diff.

# --- REVIEW CONTRACT: enforced, NOT env-overridable (hard `=`) ---
# A review must never mutate the tree. read-only lets Codex read files and run read-only git to collect
# the diff, but blocks writes. The script additionally REJECTS any value other than read-only, so this
# lens can never run write-capable even if this line is mis-edited. The model and reasoning effort are
# not here: they are the review plugin's codex_model and codex_effort settings.
CODEX_LENS_SANDBOX=read-only

# --- OPERATIONAL KNOBS — env-overridable (`:=`), cannot weaken the review ---
# Diff-context assembly threshold: for a diff within these bounds the full patch is embedded in the
# prompt; past either bound the prompt carries only the commit log + diffstat + changed-file list and
# the model is pointed at a private file holding the complete patch — keeps a huge diff from blowing
# the context window while still reviewing all of it.
: "${CODEX_LENS_MAX_INLINE_FILES:=50}"
: "${CODEX_LENS_MAX_INLINE_DIFF_BYTES:=262144}"
# Wall-clock cap (seconds) for a single review before the lens self-degrades to FAILED. A large diff's
# review is minutes; a wedged run is forever. The watchdog in scripts/codex-lens.sh caps it so an
# unattended background task never hangs. Tune against observed review durations.
: "${CODEX_LENS_TIMEOUT:=900}"
